  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "`FloatingIndicator` is designed to highlight active element in a group.\nIt can be used to create custom segmented controls, tabs and other similar components.\n\n`FloatingIndicator` renders an element over the `target` element. To calculate the position it is\nrequired to pass `parent` element which has a relative position.\n\nBy default, `FloatingIndicator` does not have any visible styles. You can use `className` prop\nor [Styles API](/styles/styles-api) to apply styles.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Multiple rows",
      "text": "`FloatingIndicator` can be used to highlight active element in a group with multiple rows:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
